# KNOWN GAP — SELF-HOST LANE ONLY (R44, routed to Track K).
# MECHANISM 1 of 3: the SH LIST arm mints its accumulator from the SOURCE
# collection's element NAME.
#
# `lower_list_comprehension` (tests/fixtures/self_host_lowerer/lower_expr.gg)
# computes `String elem_name = collection_element_type(coll_tn)` — `coll_tn` is
# the SOURCE collection's type name — and hands that to
# `collection_accumulator_tid(..., "array", elem_name, ...)`. So the result slot
# is sized and vtable'd for the SOURCE element type. The RULE, measured over a
# 39-cell grid: the SH list arm is WRONG iff the source element name differs
# from the result element name.
#     `[w for w in words]`        source String, result String  -> correct
#     `[w.len() for w in words]`  source String, result int      -> WRONG (this)
#     `[tag(n) for n in nums]`    source int,    result String   -> WRONG
#
# The RUST lane was FIXED in R44: the mint is deferred into a block left
# unterminated until the loop body has produced a MATERIALIZED element, so it
# takes the RESULT element type. Measured on the ordered Rust compiler, C and
# `--backend=llvm`: rc 0 printing `2` then `5`.
#
# ⚠ WIRED TO THE SELF-HOST LANE (`assert_self_host_stdout`), NOT `run_gg`.
# The residual is self-host-only, so a `run_gg`-wired body would be GREEN ON
# ARRIVAL — which Core #12 calls worse than no fixture — and would add a
# `scripts/known_gaps_census.sh --check` flip that
# `tests/gaps/PASSING_ALLOWLIST.txt` has no code for.
#
# ⚠ Elements are built at RUNTIME (`mk(a, b)`), never from string literals. A
# literal-backed String is a false negative here: the mis-sized 8-byte slot
# happens to hold a distinct, stable POINTER, so a broken cell reads correct.
#
# Asserts the CORRECT output. Wired test:
# `sh_comprehension_list_arm_source_derived_mint` (tests/integration.rs,
# #[ignore]d). Un-ignore when the SH list-arm mint takes the RESULT element
# type (Track K). Filed in TODO.md.
String mk(String a, String b):
    return a + b

String w0():
    return mk("alp", "ha")

String w1():
    return mk("bet", "a")

void main():
    Vector[String] words = [w0(), w1()]
    Vector[int] v = [w.len() for w in words]
    print(v.len())
    print(v.get(0).unwrap())
